### Bug Root Cause Analysis
The root cause of the bug is the inherent imprecision in JavaScript's handling of floating-point numbers. When performing arithmetic operations like addition or subtraction with floating-point numbers, the result can have more decimal places than expected due to binary representation errors. This is a common issue in many programming languages that use floating-point arithmetic.

### Bug Location
